# VEX Data Types and Conversions

## Type Hierarchy

| Type | Size | Description | Literal Example |
|------|------|-------------|-----------------|
| `int` | 4 bytes | 32-bit integer | `42`, `-1`, `0xFF` |
| `float` | 4 bytes | 32-bit float | `3.14`, `1e-5`, `.5` |
| `vector2` | 8 bytes | 2 floats | `{0.5, 0.5}` |
| `vector` | 12 bytes | 3 floats (xyz/rgb) | `{1, 2, 3}` |
| `vector4` | 16 bytes | 4 floats (quaternion/rgba) | `{0, 0, 0, 1}` |
| `matrix2` | 16 bytes | 2x2 matrix | `ident()` |
| `matrix3` | 36 bytes | 3x3 matrix (rotation/scale) | `ident()` |
| `matrix` | 64 bytes | 4x4 matrix (full transform) | `ident()` |
| `string` | varies | UTF-8 string | `"hello"` |
| `dict` | varies | Key-value dictionary | `set("k", "v")` |

## Implicit Conversions

VEX promotes types automatically in expressions:

```
int -> float -> vector2 -> vector -> vector4
                                  \-> matrix3 -> matrix
```

```vex
// int to float (automatic)
float f = 5;            // f = 5.0

// float to vector (broadcast)
vector v = 2.0;         // v = {2, 2, 2}

// int/float to vector
vector v = set(1, 2, 3);

// vector to vector4 (w=0)
vector4 q = vector4(v); // q = {v.x, v.y, v.z, 0}
```

## Explicit Conversions

```vex
// Float to int (truncate)
int i = int(3.7);            // i = 3
int i = (int)3.7;            // Same

// Int to float
float f = float(42);         // f = 42.0

// Vector component access
float x = v.x;               // or v[0]
float y = v.y;               // or v[1]
float z = v.z;               // or v[2]

// Construct vector from components
vector v = set(x, y, z);

// Vector4 component access
float w = q.w;                // or q[3]

// Matrix from vectors (columns)
matrix3 m = set(xaxis, yaxis, zaxis);

// String conversions
string s = itoa(42);         // "42"
string s = sprintf("%g", 3.14);  // "3.14"
int i = atoi("42");          // 42
float f = atof("3.14");      // 3.14

// Array type conversion
float fs[] = {1.0, 2.0, 3.0};
int is[] = {};
foreach (float f; fs) append(is, int(f));
```

## Quaternion Operations

Quaternions are stored as `vector4` with (x, y, z, w) layout:

```vex
// Identity quaternion (no rotation)
vector4 q = {0, 0, 0, 1};

// From axis-angle
vector4 q = quaternion(radians(90), {0, 1, 0});  // 90 deg around Y

// From Euler angles
vector4 q = eulertoquaternion(radians(rot), XFORM_XYZ);

// From matrix3
matrix3 m = lookat({0,0,0}, {0,0,1});
vector4 q = quaternion(m);

// Apply rotation
vector rotated = qrotate(q, @P);

// Combine rotations
vector4 q_combined = qmultiply(q1, q2);

// Interpolate (spherical)
vector4 q_blend = slerp(q1, q2, chf("blend"));

// Invert
vector4 q_inv = qinvert(q);
```

## Matrix Operations

```vex
// Identity
matrix m = ident();

// Build from components
matrix m = maketransform(XFORM_TRS, XFORM_XYZ,
    translate, rotate, scale);

// Extract components
vector t, r, s;
cracktransform(XFORM_TRS, XFORM_XYZ, {0,0,0}, m, t, r, s);

// Transform point
vector world_pos = @P * m;

// Transform direction (no translate)
matrix3 m3 = matrix3(m);
vector world_dir = @N * m3;

// Invert
matrix inv = invert(m);

// Look-at
matrix3 rot = lookat(from_pos, to_pos);

// Rotation between two vectors
matrix3 rot = dihedral(vec_a, vec_b);
```

